93	 * bytes to CipherBox Kubo, quota-gated, registering the pin row in the same
94	 * traversal. The API is zero-knowledge — it pins bytes it never inspects. Only
95	 * hosted accounts may ingress here: a BYO account pins to its own provider and
96	 * its bytes bypass the API, so a BYO upload is refused (409) rather than pinned
97	 * to hosted Kubo off the quota's books.
